  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "4845ea12-be54-4cae-9e0c-059252d2b65f",
      "phaseId": "1b6f739f-8774-4da2-af4f-5f88d0514507",
      "number": 379,
      "shortId": "7FWRN",
      "priority": 1,
      "shortName": "label-fits-its-box-truncate-en",
      "title": "Label fits its box — .truncate(End | Start), measured once",
      "status": "in-progress",
      "description": "The capability four call sites have been hand-writing.\n\n## What exists\n\n`heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/label.rs`:\n- `remeasure()` sets `width = chars × font × MONO_ADVANCE_RATIO`, `height = font × MONO_LINE_RATIO` — the label's **natural** size.\n- `paint()` draws `self.text` into `self.base.bounds` with the resolved colour/align/style, then draws decorations over the **run** (`run_rect()`), not the box.\n- Builders today: `align`, `color`, `bold`, `italic`, `underline`, `strikethrough`, `font_size`, `font_scale`, `text_signal`.\n\n`heca-grid-ui/src/style.rs`: `Layout::flex_shrink` (`None` ⇒ `0.0`) and `min_size`, with `Px(0.0)` documented at :423 as the way to allow shrinking below content size.\n\n## What to build\n\n`Label::truncate(Ellipsis)` where `Ellipsis` is `End` (labels, descriptions — cut the tail) or `Start` (paths, git branches — keep the tail, cut the head). Two behaviours together, and the second is the one that makes it work:\n\n1. **Layout**: a truncating label declares itself shrinkable — `flex_shrink = 1.0` and `min_size.width = Px(0.0)` — so the engine may hand it less than its natural width. Without this it keeps its full width and simply overflows, and the paint-time cut never triggers. This is the same trap as F003/P067's `flex_grow` lesson: a size that cannot shrink does not participate.\n2. **Paint**: fit the text to `bounds.size.w` using the *same* `MONO_ADVANCE_RATIO` cell the measure used, cutting from the end or the start and appending/prepending `…`. Cells `0` ⇒ nothing, `1` ⇒ `…` alone.\n\n`run_rect()` must follow the **drawn** text, or an underline/strikethrough would span the untruncated width.\n\n## Edge cases\n\n- Not truncating (the default) leaves `remeasure`, layout and paint exactly as they are — no existing label may move.\n- A signal-driven text that changes still re-measures; the cut is computed at paint from the current bounds, so it follows a resize with no rebuild.\n- Multi-byte text: count **chars**, never bytes (`truncate_path_left` already does).\n\n## Test (assert the drawn thing)\n\nPaint into a `Scene` and read the `DrawCommand::Text`: wide box ⇒ the full string; narrow box ⇒ a shorter string ending (or starting) in `…`; `Start` keeps the tail — `…/deep/path` — and `End` keeps the head. A test asserting only a flag is the F004 lesson repeated (a `grow` flag once passed while the layout was visibly broken); assert the text and the run rect.",
      "notes": "",
